title: What is everyone else doing here?
model: sonnet
effort: low
system: Read-only session: look with gh and git; change nothing, push nothing, comment on nothing. Running git fetch is allowed.

Tell me what other people are doing in this repository. Leave my own work out except where it collides with theirs. I am whoever `gh api user --jq .login` prints.

Report in this order, and say "none" for an empty section:

1. Their open pull requests: number, author, what it is for in one line, review state, checks.
2. Branches someone else pushed in the last two weeks that have no pull request.
3. What was merged since my last commit on the default branch, and by whom.
4. What is waiting on me: reviews requested from me, issues assigned to me.
5. Overlap: any of their pull requests or branches touching files changed on the branches my tabs are on (`git worktree list` shows them), or paths an open claim in `claude-peer log show` names.

End with the one thing I should look at first.
